  "threads": {
    "46354088": {
      "id": "46354088",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:39:49.220Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "This hands back Shopify's URL, but nothing receives Shopify's callback: no endpoint stores the new token, sets the store connected, and re-sends the held refunds. Settings, reconnected promises all three."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:41:28.859Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Added GET /shopify/callback: verifies Shopify's HMAC and our signed state, saves the token, sets the store connected and publishes refund.requested for each held refund. This endpoint now only hands out the URL with that state."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "post-store-shopify-reconnect"
    },
    "05c0a0b2": {
      "id": "05c0a0b2",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:29:41.386Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "It says buyers pick up branding within an hour, but nothing caches it. Either cache what the buyer page reads of the store (and drop it on save), or say changes show at once."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:30:01.162Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Went with showing changes at once: the lookup already reads stores and load is a few requests a second, so a cache would only add a way to be wrong. Updated the summary, the PublicStore note and the Settings header."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:30:16.436Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Decided: No cache on store settings; buyers see changes on their next lookup"
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "patch-store"
    },
    "06879cbc": {
      "id": "06879cbc",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:47:05.932Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Say what the buyer sees when the order is older than the return window"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:47:57.096Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Added a Window closed state on Find your order: the 410 shows when the window closed and what the buyer can still do."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "post-orders-lookup"
    },
    "0c893fc9": {
      "id": "0c893fc9",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T20:54:56.663Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Its buttons are now uses of the Buttons set (Tone: Accent | Danger, Weight: Solid | Outline): Refund is Accent solid, Reject is Danger outline, and in Rejecting the send button is Danger solid. Looks the same; one place to change them from now on."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "c297162d"
    },
    "48e512a2": {
      "id": "48e512a2",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:03:47.127Z",
          "author": "claude-code",
          "body": "Should a merchant be able to refund before the parcel arrives (trusted buyers, damaged items they don't want back)? Right now 422 blocks it."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:03:47.343Z",
          "author": "reviewer",
          "body": "Not for v1: refunds wait for the parcel. Revisit with a per-store 'refund on label scan' setting."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "post-returns-id-refund"
    },
    "68723c6c": {
      "id": "68723c6c",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:39:49.025Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Step 2 sets status refunding, but ReturnStatus has no refunding (the Refund retrying screen shows it too). Add it to the enum, or name the status this step really sets."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:41:15.628Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Added refunding to ReturnStatus: approved and queued, not yet confirmed by Shopify. The trace and the Refund retrying screen now agree with it."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "refund-a-return"
    },
    "6d1ebd91": {
      "id": "6d1ebd91",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:39:48.650Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Two gaps. It hears return.rejected, but its Resend link carries only the refund-sent email, so the reason never reaches the buyer. And when Shopify refuses the token (401), nothing sets stores.shopify_status to needs_reconnect, so Settings never shows the disconnected state; say it holds the job and marks the store."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:40:17.727Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Worker now emails the rejection with the reason (Resend link), and on a Shopify 401 marks the store needs_reconnect and holds the job instead of retrying; its purpose says both."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "refund-worker"
    },
    "7b3056a8": {
      "id": "7b3056a8",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:38:15.227Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Should a rejected return email the buyer a reason, or just the status?"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T17:39:03.626Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Decided: Email the reason the merchant gave; buyers asked why"
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "post-returns-id-reject"
    },
    "80bf3d05": {
      "id": "80bf3d05",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:39:48.834Z",
          "author": "you",
          "body": "Reject sends a reason the buyer reads, but no column keeps it: add rejection_reason. Related: refunds has no amount, so a partial refund's amount lives nowhere."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T18:41:15.327Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Added returns.rejection_reason (personal: merchants may quote the buyer). refunds now keeps amount and currency, the amount actually paid; returns.refund_amount stays what the items cost, the most a refund can be."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "returns"
    },
    "9214aa0f": {
      "id": "9214aa0f",
      "posts": [
        {
          "at": "2026-10-03T20:34:16.256Z",
          "author": "codex",
          "body": "Works at 768 now: sections stack to one column, the sidebar narrows to 184 px, and Save never wraps. Same in both states."
        }
      ],
      "state": "resolved",
      "target": "8ab55488"
    }
  },
